# 4E-BP / eIF4F model, reference parameter set (Table 1 of the manuscript).
# All bimolecular constants nM^-1 s^-1, unimolecular s^-1, concentrations nM.
# Thermodynamic constraints satisfied by this set: one common cycle ratio for the four
# ATP-driven PdP cycles (ln Gamma = 19.8), balanced scaffold loop (Gamma_M4 = 1),
# association constants <= 0.1 nM^-1 s^-1, affinities in the reported ranges (Section 2.2).
# Numbers identical to MATLAB/model/p4e_ref.m (rebinding constants rounded to 6 significant digits).
# File: NetworkODE_PdP1.ode   (Fig 2A): one dual phosphorylation cycle with the rate constants of the first cycle, R1-R8 (Thr37/Thr46),
# coupled to eIF4E release (R17, from the doubly phosphorylated complex) and 4E-BP rebinding (R22). No scaffold.

# S0 = BPe4E, S1 = BPe4Ep, S2 = BPe4Epp (doubly phosphorylated in this reduced model)
P = Pt - (C3 + C4)
kin = kint - (C1 + C2)
e4E = e4Et - (BPe4E + BPe4Ep + BPe4Epp + C1 + C2 + C3 + C4)
BP = BPt - (BPe4E + BPe4Ep + BPe4Epp + BPp + C1 + C2 + C3 + C4)
r1 = ka1*BPe4E*kin - kd1*C1
r2 = ka2*C1 - kd2*BPe4Ep*kin
r3 = ka3*BPe4Ep*kin - kd3*C2
r4 = ka4*C2 - kd4*BPe4Epp*kin
r5 = ka5*BPe4Epp*P - kd5*C3
r6 = ka6*C3 - kd6*BPe4Ep*P
r7 = ka7*BPe4Ep*P - kd7*C4
r8 = ka8*C4 - kd8*BPe4E*P
r17 = kf17*BPe4Epp - kb17*e4E*BPp
r22 = kf22*BP*e4E - kb22*BPe4E
param kint=1
param e4Et=1000, BPt=4500, Pt=41
# constants of the first cycle, R1-R8 (Thr37/Thr46) (ka/kd = forward/backward of the cycle's eight steps)
param ka1=0.031, kd1=0.11, ka2=0.0029, kd2=1.8118e-08
param ka3=0.1, kd3=0.032, ka4=17, kd4=5.24819e-06
param ka5=0.023, kd5=0.63, ka6=0.027, kd6=2.51194e-05
param ka7=0.03, kd7=5.5, ka8=0.14, kd8=8.67184e-08
param kf17=10, kb17=0.00204082, kf22=0.1, kb22=0.5
BPe4Epp' = r4 - r5 - r17
C1' = r1 - r2
BPe4Ep' = r2 - r3 + r6 - r7
C2' = r3 - r4
C3' = r5 - r6
C4' = r7 - r8
BPp' = r17
BPe4E' = -r1 + r8 + r22
init BPe4E=1000
aux free_e4E = e4E

@ meth=cvode, tol=1e-9, atol=1e-9, total=300000, dt=50, maxstor=100000
@ bounds=1e12, xp=t, yp=BPe4E, xlo=0, xhi=300000, ylo=0, yhi=1100
# AUTO: start from a steady state at small kint (integrate first), then continue in kint
@ parmin=0.5, parmax=1000, autoxmin=0, autoxmax=600, autoymin=0, autoymax=1100
@ Nmax=20000, NPr=500, Ds=0.02, Dsmin=1e-6, Dsmax=1, Normmax=1e8, epss=1e-7, epsl=1e-8, epsu=1e-8
done
